@RigForge_HostAddress = https://localhost:7280

### Register (stores the token for the requests below)
POST {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "tester@rigforge.dev",
  "username": "tester",
  "password": "secret1",
  "confirmPassword": "secret1"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Login (stores the token for the requests below)
POST {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "tester@rigforge.dev",
  "password": "secret1"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Health check (no auth)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/health

### Current user (stores userId)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

> {% client.global.set("userId", response.body.user.id); %}

### List builds (newest first)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds?page=1&pageSize=12

### List builds (search title/CPU/GPU + purpose + price range + sort)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds?search=rtx&purpose=Gaming&minPrice=1000&maxPrice=2500&sort=MostLiked

### Create build (needs build.jpg next to this file; returns 201 with no body)
POST {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=RigForgeBoundary

--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

My Gaming Rig
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="purpose"

Gaming
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cpu"

AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="gpu"

NVIDIA RTX 4070 Super
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ram"

32GB DDR5 6000
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="storage"

2TB NVMe SSD
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="psu"

Corsair RM850x
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="priceEur"

1849.99
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A quiet 1440p gaming build with plenty of headroom for upgrades.
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="build.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./build.jpg
--RigForgeBoundary--

### My builds / a user's profile builds (stores your newest build's id as buildId)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/users/{{userId}}/builds?page=1&pageSize=12

> {% client.global.set("buildId", response.body.items[0].id); %}

### Build details
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update build (image is optional; omit it to keep the current one)
PUT {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=RigForgeBoundary

--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

My Gaming Rig v2
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="purpose"

Gaming
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="cpu"

AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="gpu"

NVIDIA RTX 4080 Super
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ram"

32GB DDR5 6000
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="storage"

2TB NVMe SSD
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="psu"

Corsair RM1000x
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="priceEur"

2299.00
--RigForgeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Upgraded the GPU and PSU for 4K. Still quiet under load.
--RigForgeBoundary--

### Like build
POST {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}/like
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unlike build
DELETE {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}/like
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add comment
POST {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Great airflow on this one!"
}

### List comments for a build (stores the newest comment's id as commentId)
GET {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}/comments?page=1&pageSize=12

> {% client.global.set("commentId", response.body.items[0].id); %}

### Edit comment
PUT {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Great airflow and cable management!"
}

### Delete comment
DELETE {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete build
DELETE {{RigForge_HostAddress}}/api/builds/{{buildId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
